WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.430
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.771
How are you today?

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.740
I'm feeling great.

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.351
Look what I have.

5
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.560
It's full of weather pictures.

6
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.960
Whoa , my weather pictures are everywhere.

7
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.250
Does a snowman need sunglasses?

8
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:25.920
That looks silly.

9
00:00:27.241 --> 00:00:29.701
And why is this umbrella over the sun?

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.000
These pictures are all mixed up. Can you help me put them in the right places?

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.540
Fantastic. Let's play weather match.

12
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.680
First, let's get everything ready.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.670
We need our weather match worksheet.

14
00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:51.750
Look, we have sunny, rainy, and snowy.

15
00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.261
We also need scissors.

16
00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.801
Please use your scissors carefully.

17
00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:04.740
Ask your teacher for help if you need it. And we need some glue.

18
00:01:06.571 --> 00:01:07.560
Do you have everything?

19
00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.520
Worksheet, scissors, and glue.

20
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.610
Great, we're ready.

21
00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.140
First, we need to cut out all the pictures.

22
00:01:20.461 --> 00:01:23.190
Look at the pictures on the right side of your worksheet.

23
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.280
We have nine pictures.

24
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:32.160
Cut carefully along the dotted lines, nice and slowly.

25
00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.870
Keep going. Cut carefully.

26
00:01:38.279 --> 00:01:39.240
Take your time.

27
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.330
Now, spread out your pictures so you can see them all. Are you finished?

28
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.950
Wonderful. Put your scissors down safely.

29
00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.180
Before we start, let's look at our weather.

30
00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.700
This is sunny.

31
00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.711
Say it with me.

32
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:00.601
Sunny.

33
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.220
This is rainy.

34
00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.020
Rainy.

35
00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.300
And this is snowy.

36
00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.130
Snowy.

37
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.400
Sunny, rainy, snowy. Excellent.

38
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.130
I'll show you how to play.

39
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.500
Look at this picture.

40
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.110
What is it?

41
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.830
It's the sun.

42
00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.410
Where does the sun go?

43
00:02:53.851 --> 00:02:56.130
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

44
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.710
The sun shines brightly in sunny weather.

45
00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.410
It goes in sunny.

46
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.530
Put a little glue on the worksheet,

47
00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.040
then stick it in the sunny column.

48
00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.240
Great. Now let's do the other pictures together.

49
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.180
Find the umbrella.

50
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.740
Here it is.

51
00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.150
We hold an umbrella when water falls from the sky.

52
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.610
Where does it go?

53
00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.270
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

54
00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:44.550
It goes in rainy.

55
00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.650
Put some glue on the worksheet and stick it in the rainy column.

56
00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.570
Great matching.

57
00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.951
Now, find the snowman.

58
00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:12.421
Hello, snowman. We make a snowman when there is lots of snow.

59
00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:17.820
Where does it go? Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

60
00:04:24.841 --> 00:04:26.160
It goes in snowy.

61
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.970
Glue the snowman in the snowy column.

62
00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.000
Fantastic.

63
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.230
Find the sunglasses.

64
00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:51.600
Ooh, very cool. We wear sunglasses when the sun is bright.

65
00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.430
Where do they go?

66
00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.820
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

67
00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.370
They go in sunny.

68
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.120
Glue the sunglasses in the sunny column.

69
00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.201
Excellent work.

70
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.830
Next, find the snowflake.

71
00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:31.470
A snowflake is cold and blue. Does it go in sunny, rainy,

72
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:32.520
or snowy?

73
00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.040
It goes in snowy.

74
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.790
Glue the snowflake in the snowy column.

75
00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:51.720
Wonderful.

76
00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.410
Find the rain boots.

77
00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.360
We wear rain boots to keep our feet dry. Where do they go?

78
00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.540
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

79
00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.760
They go in rainy.

80
00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.390
Glue the rain boots in the rainy column.

81
00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.349
Nice job.

82
00:06:31.561 --> 00:06:33.480
Now, find the sunhat.

83
00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.570
Can you see it?

84
00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.170
There it is.

85
00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:46.440
A sunhat protects us from the bright sun. Where does it go?

86
00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.710
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

87
00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.050
It goes in sunny.

88
00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.010
Glue the sunhat in the sunny column.

89
00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:08.730
Great job.

90
00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.600
Find the sled.

91
00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:23.760
We ride a sled over the snow. Wee! Where does it go?

92
00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.210
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

93
00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.820
It goes in snowy.

94
00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.360
Glue the sled in the snowy column.

95
00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.030
Snow-tastic.

96
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:53.701
We have one picture left. Find the raincoat.

97
00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:03.480
A raincoat keeps us dry when it rains. Where does it go?

98
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.811
Sunny, rainy, or snowy?

99
00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:18.780
It goes in rainy. Glue the raincoat in the rainy column.

100
00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.260
You did it.

101
00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.120
Let's do one quick weather challenge.

102
00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.470
Umbrella, sunny, rainy, or snowy?

103
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.040
Rainy.

104
00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:46.590
Sunhat, sunny, rainy, or snowy?

105
00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:53.190
Sunny.

106
00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:58.651
Snowman, sunny, rainy, or snowy?

107
00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.370
Snowy.

108
00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:10.170
Amazing. You remembered everything.

109
00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:16.530
You did a wonderful job today. You cut out the pictures, thought

110
00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:20.190
carefully, and matched every picture with the right weather.

111
00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:22.920
Give yourself a big clap.

112
00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:29.700
Thank you for playing weather match with me. See you next time. Bye-bye.
